0042-mods-state-export-copy-picker-guard.patch -- three silent degradations of the app's own state and copies (docs/REVIEW-TRIAGE-2026-11-19.md, finding 4.9).
Applied by scripts/build-app.sh to its copy of the C# snapshot (patch -p1, run in the project folder), after 0041; app/gameapp/ is not edited.
UNTESTED ON DEVICE: written without a C# compiler. The fourth item of 4.9 (a passphrase longer than the shim's buffer) is in app/gameapp_shim_rust.c and the Rust side, not here.
  * GameAppMods.cs: ReadState swallowed ANY read error and returned the empty state, and the first toggle then wrote that empty state over the real file: the player's mod / patch / cheat
    choices were lost for good. ReadState (showing, the build) is unchanged; SetMod / SetPatch / SetCheat / Delete / Import now read with ReadStateForUpdate, which treats a missing file as empty
    but lets a failing read of an existing file throw, before anything is changed. GameAppModsUi.cs shows that error ("Not changed") instead of letting a switch handler throw.
  * GameAppExport.cs PreparePlayerDocuments (first launch of an exported player): a file is copied as <name>.part and renamed, so a copy that stops half way never leaves a truncated file under
    its real name (which the next launches, seeing the name, skipped as already set up).
  * GameAppMain.cs TakeCertificateBytes: the picker's copy of the .p12 is deleted so the certificate never stays in a file, but the test was "the path is under HOME", true for every file of the
    container, including a .p12 the player had put in Documents/ and picked from there. Now only the container's tmp/ (where Import mode puts the copy) and Documents/Inbox/ qualify.
